d turbulent  history together ripe for the picking  and in this scene there's plenty of  nuance present that i liked and i  touched on it earlier from sakura's  point of view she sees naruto as someone  that's trapped in his own fantasy a  person she deeply cares about has a love  for her which forces him to take  increasingly more extreme action putting  himself into life-threatening danger she  thinks that's her perspective and  believing that's the reality sakura  feels a tremendous amount of guilt and  responsibility to alleviate that stress  and that's a really cool idea and what  makes it even better is naruto's  response to that  [Music]  this is one of the best decisions made  not only in this arc but perhaps some of  the most important thematic and  character defining lines heading into  this big climax with moderate  highlighting for us as an audience how  naruto handles and doesn't handle every  piece of news that comes his way earlier  in this arc madura expresses to the  world leaders what his ultimate goals  were to seize control over everyone's  autonomy using infinite tsukuyomi the  infinite tsukuyomi is an extremely  powerful genjutsu that traps the entire  world in what is effectively an illusion  enslaving the human population in a  dream so that their chakra may be drawn  upon by the god tree or at least that's  what it says on narutopedia it is in  effect a technique which traps the  victim in a fantasy a delusion and in  the scenes where naruto is forced to  contend with the fantasy and delusion  sakura offers him that he has always  wanted he unflinchingly chooses reality  the more difficult option to not live in  a lie because as he says he hates those  people the responsibility to trudge  forward no matter how hard reality can  be and as we can see it can be extremely  difficult particularly for him and  that's what this arc is all about in a  sense with regards cell 7 or team 7.  each character is at their most  desperate made evident by the crazy  decision sakura made the length sasuke  is willing to go to and obviously with  the way naruto's circumstances are  causing him to feel gone are the days of  childhood concerns and vapid spats we  are on the cusp of war and we feel that  with each subsequent page turn and so  putting a pin on this sakura scene there  are clearly some interesting ideas and  profoundly interesting thematic choices  made that speak wonderfully to the  character of naruto and in some ways  sakura however all of this good i think  really came at the cost of any and all  respect i had for the sakura character  as a competent and level-headed ninja  now time for something completely  different kisame versus killer b is  pretty damn cool i honestly had no idea  kasami could transform like that i mean  was it hinted at before or was it a  surprise for people let me know down  below i'm actually not sure about that  in addition to that i think what i like  most about this fight is what it meant  for this series moving forward this  second form and indeed even the tail  forms killer b utilizes are nothing new  to the series however what's interesting  here is that killer bee seems to be in  complete control of this form and with  that it makes me wonder if naruto will  have to learn how to do the same it  seems like the natural final training  arc for him to undergo on his way to big  final battle i mean it's literally him  mastering the demon inside of him it's a  cool concept but who knows maybe this  speculation is a complete waste of time  the fight itself is really cool with  kisame breaking out a sword that can  suck chakra which comes in handy later  in the fight but moreover as it looks  like he's about to win against killer  bee reikage shows up and then the two  brothers just decapitate kisame which i  wasn't expecting although now that we're  heading towards the end game it makes  sense to nick some characters here and  there  and speaking of nixing some characters  it's ti